Agents are an abstraction over bots
Agents are managed by the user
Bots are managed by the pooler

When the simulator starts up, the pooler should create some number of bots. This is the bot pool

Whenever the user creates an agent, they should at some point ask the pooler to bind a bot to it.
The pooler should check the bot pool for a free bot. If a free bot exists, the pooler should bind that bot and return success.
    If there is no free bot available, the pooler should return failure.

Whenever the user is done with an agent (not necessarily when they die!), they should ask the pooler to unbind that agent's bot.
The pooler should set the agent's bot to None, return that bot to the pool, and reset that bot's inventory, health, hunger, etc.

